MSSL{
α≡{"format":"0.3","profile":"basic_mssl.executable.3","record":"MSSL.Document","source_language":"MSSL","source_version":"0.3"},
ι≡"mssl:rinkvt:lkvexa:engine:2.5.0-lkvexa.3",
λ≡"rinkvt.lkvexa.engine",
ℛ≡{"0001":"module(\"rinkvt.lkvexa.engine\")","0002":"learn(\"component\",literal(\"engine/ (33 modules and 3 data tables: the reference edition's engine 2.5.0-rinkvt.1 with the start frame, the whistle and the league overtime rules of this release), ui/loader.js, ui/app.js\"))","0003":"learn(\"contract\",literal(\"the command language, frames, game actor, models, roster importer and HK001 run in the renderer as the reference edition runs them; the window sends the host every change a command made and shows the command's result only after the host has it on disk; when the host refuses, the window loads the league again\"))","0004":"learn(\"engine_version\",literal(\"2.5.0-rinkvt.1+startframe+whistle+overtime\"))","0005":"learn(\"start_frame\",literal(\"START is the game's start frame, a !CLK frame with the action byte 66 (B): the opening faceoff. In a game created under the start-frame rule, as every game created in this edition is, the clock runs only after it and GO is refused until then; a game created by an earlier build starts with its first GO, so its ledger replays unchanged\"))","0006":"learn(\"whistle\",literal(\"WHISTLE is the whistle, a !CLK frame with the action byte 87 (W): it stops the running clock and play is dead until the faceoff. WHISTLE mm:ss also sets the clock to the time on the official clock when the whistle went; on a clock a whistle already stopped it sets that whistle's time, on a clock STOP stopped it makes the stoppage a whistle. It is refused before the clock has run in the period, in the shootout, and (without a time) on a stopped clock. Esc in the workbench is the whistle while the clock runs; every whistle is counted on the scoreboard\"))","0007":"learn(\"overtime_rules\",literal(\"a league's overtime rules (rink overtime LEAGUE preset | ot= skaters= shootout= playoff-ot= playoff-skaters= playoff-shootout= | clear) decide a game that is level after regulation: the overtime's length (none, or 1:00 to 20:00), skaters a side (3, 4 or 5), shootout rounds (none, or 1 to 10, then sudden death); a regular block for regular-season and preseason games, a playoff block for playoff and championship games, where no shootout means sudden-death periods up to OT9. Presets: standard, four-on-four, international, overtime-then-tie, shootout-only, ties. Each game keeps a copy of its league's rules from its creation (the home team's league, else the away team's); a game without one keeps the built-in rules, exactly as earlier builds played it. A tie that stands earns a point each\"))","0008":"learn(\"ja_contract\",literal(\"[\\\"contracts/ja/rinkvt_frame.ja\\\",\\\"contracts/ja/rinkvt_overtime.ja\\\"]\"))","0009":"learn(\"maturity\",literal(\"OPERATIONAL\"))","0010":"learn(\"evidence\",literal(\"[\\\"tests/test_browser.py\\\",\\\"tests/test_store.py\\\"]\"))","0011":"learn(\"scope_limit\",literal(\"the engine's own test suite belongs to the reference edition (Node.js), whose 78 engine tests pass on this engine, and whose 128 other tests pass with it; this edition exercises the engine through its browser tests\"))"},
π≡[],
δ≡11,
τ≡0,
